:: Lord's Rest - Main Road
<<if $pendingTownWakeMessage>>
<<print $pendingTownWakeMessage>>
<<set $pendingTownWakeMessage = "">>

<</if>>

Snow-covered roads narrow into a dirt path someone still takes the time to clear.

A lit mansion waits at the end, behind a steel gate tall enough to make its point without help.

The world ended years ago. Someone swept the road this morning.

[[Gate|Lord's Rest - Gate]]

<<link "Leave">>
  <<run setup.enterMap("G")>>
<</link>>

:: Lord's Rest - Gate
<<if $lordsRest.daughterRescued and !$lordsRest.accessGranted>>
A young woman stands beside you, bruised and hungry but alive.

The guards have not seen her yet.

<</if>>

A steel gate cuts across the road. Two guards stand beneath it.

The bars are bent and bruised in places, but they still stand.

They have seen their share of monsters. The guards look much the same.

[[Guard|Lord's Rest - Guard]]

<<if $lordsRest.accessGranted>>
[[Main House|Lord's Rest - Main House]]
<</if>>

<<if $lordsRest.pleaded and !$clearedDungeons.lordsRestGoblinCamp and $lordsRest.accessMethod isnot "bribe">>
<<link "Goblin Camp">>
  <<run setup.openDungeonWarning("lordsRestGoblinCamp", "Lord's Rest - Gate")>>
<</link>>
<</if>>

[[Main Road|Lord's Rest - Main Road]]

:: Lord's Rest - Guard
<<if $lordsRest.daughterRescued and !$lordsRest.accessGranted>>
The guard sees the spear first. Then he sees his daughter.

"Oh, thank God."

He reaches for her, thinks better of it for half a second, then holds her anyway.

"Those goblins took my only daughter. Thank you. I mean it."

He looks at the gate.

"The gate is open to you."

<<run setup.completeLordsRestCampQuest()>>

[[Main House|Lord's Rest - Main House]]

[[Leave|Lord's Rest - Gate]]

<<elseif $lordsRest.accessGranted and $lordsRest.accessMethod is "camp">>
"Thank you again. Let me know if there is anything you need."

[[Main House|Lord's Rest - Main House]]

[[Leave|Lord's Rest - Gate]]

<<elseif $lordsRest.accessGranted and $lordsRest.accessMethod is "bribe">>
The guard glances at his coat.

"Go on, then."

[[Main House|Lord's Rest - Main House]]

[[Leave|Lord's Rest - Gate]]

<<else>>
"Halt! Who goes there?"

[...]

"A traveler?"

[...]

"Unfortunately, we cannot take guests right now, sir."

<<link "Bribe — 20 gold">>
  <<run setup.bribeLordsRestGuard()>>
<</link>>

<<link "Plead">>
  <<run setup.pleadWithLordsRestGuard()>>
<</link>>

[[Leave|Lord's Rest - Gate]]
<</if>>

:: Lord's Rest - Guard Plea
"I cannot let anyone in right now. There may be a way to change that."

"A goblin camp has been growing east of here. We can hear them at night now."

"I do not know if this gate will hold without casualties."

"Kill their chief and bring me his spear. Do that, and I will let you through."

<<link "Goblin Camp">>
  <<run setup.openDungeonWarning("lordsRestGoblinCamp", "Lord's Rest - Gate")>>
<</link>>

[[Leave|Lord's Rest - Gate]]

:: Lord's Rest - Main House
Warm air meets you at the door. You had almost forgotten it could do that.

Fires burn beneath clean mantels. Someone has scrubbed the mud from the floor recently.

The end of the world has been asked to wipe its feet before coming in.

[[Steward|Lord's Rest - Steward]]

[[Gardens|Lord's Rest - Gardens]]

[[Fields|Lord's Rest - Fields]]

[[Gate|Lord's Rest - Gate]]

:: Lord's Rest - Steward
<<if $lordsRest.accessMethod is "camp">>
"The guard told us what you did."

The steward studies you for a moment.

"He told us several times. I expect he will keep doing so."
<<else>>
"The guard said you made an arrangement."

The steward glances toward the gate.

"He used a more respectable word for it."
<</if>>

[[Main House|Lord's Rest - Main House]]

:: Lord's Rest - Gardens
Winter roses grow between dark hedges. Someone has cleared every path through the snow.

Maintaining a garden after the end of the world feels unreasonable. That may be why they keep doing it.

[[Groundskeeper|Lord's Rest - Groundskeeper]]

[[Main House|Lord's Rest - Main House]]

[[Fields|Lord's Rest - Fields]]

:: Lord's Rest - Groundskeeper
The groundskeeper cuts a dead branch from a rosebush.

"People think the cold kills them."

Another branch falls. "Mostly, people do."

[[Gardens|Lord's Rest - Gardens]]

:: Lord's Rest - Fields
Black soil breaks through the snow in long, narrow rows.

Canvas shelters bend over the winter crops. Workers move between them with numb hands and practiced steps.

The mansion eats because these people do not stop.

[[Farmhand|Lord's Rest - Farmhand]]

[[Main House|Lord's Rest - Main House]]

[[Gardens|Lord's Rest - Gardens]]

:: Lord's Rest - Farmhand
The farmhand tucks both hands beneath their arms.

"The ground is frozen."

They look across the rows. "It has not noticed that we need it."

[[Fields|Lord's Rest - Fields]]

